<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Culture &amp; Lifestyle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:04Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-cul" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1441?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israeli minister accuses 'NAZA' filmmakers of 'treason'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf3815b770e5d6fdb2f06e5c7bb6882bd426ef6579fb26497bf150f219369666</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-minister-accuses-naza-filmmakers-of-treason/a-79255860--3831f9d14cfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-minister-accuses-naza-filmmakers-of-treason/a-79255860?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israel's culture minister wants to strip the makers of a documentary on Israel's Gaza offensive of their citizenship. He accused the two of seeking "applause from antisemites around the world."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The Crusades: How a medieval Holy War still shapes politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9459e2800eb6539c1412a3cbf66f463c1ade39c794e5c75b4dcd004e3ced6471</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-crusades-how-a-medieval-holy-war-still-shapes-politics/a-79203784--8fa07b173177.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-crusades-how-a-medieval-holy-war-still-shapes-politics/a-79203784?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 1095, the Catholic Church launched the Crusades: wars that left millions dead and whose legacy still shapes political and ideological conflicts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Russians on the Goethe-Institut: 'Hostage to politics'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f560cf7779b676b578cef21078c8d7802b74661885a9ad758460cb6d9adcf56</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936--8619b68c7998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia has affected their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The 'end of an era' as Goethe-Institut in Russia closes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a88a3b7a725a2df42d1e7f7aaf1a25496246a9b035150131735cf1348726f0d</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321--189393464061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Goethe-Institut was one of the last German institutions still operating in Russia. However, following Moscow's decision to close its offices, all employees will have to stop working by September 13.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Belarusians still find hope in a silenced country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dff7bfc9eaacb32a829782d22e1c2ee5e86bd149b2bfd76e1e3ff5dafaa0f008</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285--d234556fa838.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The documentary "Letters from the Silenced Country" depicts the ongoing repression under the authoritarian regime. Director Andrei Kutsila talked to DW ahead of the film's Venice premiere.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>A Romani artist in Hungary reclaims his identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:866143f71a732e0cfdb8371dda765fb52221c7247ade5f2bd606b650345a9cbe</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266--3fed9cef9147.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Norbert Olah is an artist. He's also Romani. For a long time, he avoided making his ethnic background a theme of his art for fear of being pigeonholed. Then it became his focus.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How Celine Dion became a pop culture icon across generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ade1703fa556e477a198ae0171b2c0f0bc2c35aeeca1012bc4ca2466aba8bd7</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-celine-dion-became-a-pop-culture-icon-across-generations/a-79213779--40db204d1ea8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-celine-dion-became-a-pop-culture-icon-across-generations/a-79213779?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the global star kicks off her anticipated Paris residency, here's how Celine Dion managed to gain younger followers while keeping her loyal older fans.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae1210e49270c6443f47d2f6eb7020abe60c30ab8dd1ec06f4c6aaf45ab8ee69</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:03Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--1ca180b39c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Pay to ghost your boss: Japan's resignation business</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcb0f83845acf5a3d77e57853164a016ee2d9cea82e0e0f74b778b296e40a471</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584--1937a091cd92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Resignation agencies in Japan help employees leave their jobs seamlessly in just 15 minutes. Young people are especially eager to use their services.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: CDU ahead in Lower Saxony local election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72be9d08ed392ac7022ddf42792f155e9085d8e515fda81e0d5faded7754f244</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T00:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-ahead-in-lower-saxony-local-election/live-79223427--aff1c7ebec22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-ahead-in-lower-saxony-local-election/live-79223427?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The CDU is on course to win in municipal polls in the northwestern state of Lower Saxony that were seen as a gauge of support for the far-right AfD party.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb2ae01da0f689c349308c3c5aff89bb5f7de34bcee901147b7d544677753388</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Bauhaus Manifesto: Broad alliance promoting artistic freedom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcf63999e9251109eee8f22b2ec5abab8708c60530014dedd1caf446812da8b8</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:03Z</updated><published>2026-08-21T10:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bauhaus-manifesto-broad-alliance-promoting-artistic-freedom/a-78456460--2d3d86ae9554.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bauhaus-manifesto-broad-alliance-promoting-artistic-freedom/a-78456460?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Weeks before Saxony-Anhalt's state election, representatives from German cultural, crafts, architecture, design and church sectors unite to promote freedom, openness and creativity.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
